 behavior_note='The Empero size comparison is a precision/coverage tradeoff under this fixed prompt: '+ '; '.join(empty)+'. The larger files often return no memories even when the turn has reference facts. Empty arrays are schema-valid and write zero facts; they are not syntax failures. These counts explain the immediate recall loss, not why the weights abstain. Prompt/template sensitivity and weight behavior are not separated. [Descriptive empty-output audit](v2/results/writer-behavior.json).'
 coder_note='Edited minus stock: validity '+delta(2,'valid_rate')+', precision '+delta(2,'precision')+', and recall '+delta(2,'recall')+'. The edited artifact completed more outputs but wrote fewer facts and covered fewer references; the precision interval spans both directions. These are file-level comparisons, not isolated editing effects.'
 fix_note=f"On the general-schema task, default 4B completed {models['qwen3.5-4b-q4_k_m']['valid']}/900 outputs and repeat-1.1 completed {models['qwen3.5-4b-q4_k_m-repeat-1.1']['valid']}/900; repeat-1.1 minus default recall was "+delta(3,'recall')+'. The narrow-prompt repair is therefore not a blanket recommendation for the general writer prompt.'

